## Steer 2 — resume from the 01:30 stall (contract derivation defect fixed)

### D1 — Contract was hand-mirroring the database (defect, fixed)

The first billing contract hand-wrote every `z.object`/`z.enum` while its header claimed the
schemas were "derived from the database schemas" — a claim `git diff` falsified. Fixed:

- `contracts/versions/v1/billing.contract.ts` now derives every entity schema from the generated
  Prisma-Zod models (`@database/zod` → `CustomerSchema`, `InvoiceSchema`, `InvoiceLineSchema`,
  `PaymentSchema`, `CreditNoteSchema`, `CreditLedgerEntrySchema`, `EntitlementGrantSchema`,
  `PlanSchema`, `PlanVersionSchema`, `PlanComponentSchema`, `MeterSchema`,
  `SubscriptionSchema`) via `.pick({...})` + `.extend(...)`: the database owns field existence,
  enum values and nullability; the contract narrows where the public surface is stricter
  (string-encoded money over `z.custom(isDecimalLike)`, ISO strings over `z.date()`, bounded
  strings, email format) and hand-writes only envelopes, computed projections
  (`pendingChangeId`, `customerName`, `revoked`, tier parsing, detail aggregations) and the two
  serialization encodings (`MoneySchemaV1`, `IsoDateTimeSchemaV1`).
- Public filter enums are DB-derived too: `Database<X>Schema.shape.<field>.removeDefault()`
  (and `.unwrap().unwrap()` for the wrapped `RunDecision`) — no `z.enum([...])` in the contract
  hand-mirrors a database enum any more. If the table's enum changes, the contract fails to
  compile against the new values.
- `contracts/versions/v1/runs.contract.ts` derives `RunSchemaV1`/`RunItemSchemaV1` from
  `BillingRunSchema`/`RunItemSchema` the same way; `RunStatusV1Schema`,
  `RunItemStatusV1Schema`, `ExceptionBucketV1Schema`, and the decision enum all come from the
  generated models.
- Two framework facts learned by asking (see ledger below) shaped the fix:
  `@netscript/contracts` helpers (`paginationLimit`, `boundedString`, …) return structural
  `ContractSchema` values that cannot be chained (`.optional()`) inside zod envelopes — the
  framework's own generated contracts keep plain zod in envelopes — and `paginationLimit` in a
  zod envelope degraded the handler's inferred `input.limit` to `{}`, so envelopes keep plain
  zod bounds.
- `classifyException` now returns the generated `ExceptionBucket` type (imported from the
  generated client), closing the string→enum mismatch that produced the TS2322 on
  `exceptionBucket` in the run pipeline.
- `comparePercentDelta` was rewritten on `parseMoney` micros instead of `Number()` on money
  strings (float-free delta; percent threshold check kept).

### D2 — Runs service completed (the mid-task stall)

The stall left `services/runs` referencing files that did not exist and a scaffold-era router.
Completed:

- `lib/billing-client.ts` — typed client to the billing service (Aspire discovery).
- `lib/stream.ts` — run console durable stream: `defineStreamSchema` +
  `createServiceStreamProducer` (the Service-facing producer from `@netscript/plugin-streams-core`,
  resolving `DURABLE_STREAMS_URL`/`services__streams__http__0`), `publishRunConsole(runId,
  status)` upserts a transition event and flushes; best-effort (logged, never fails a run).
- `domain/pipeline.ts` — the issue path now triggers worker jobs through the real workers
  contract surface: `workersClient.triggerJob({ id, payload, correlationId })` (flat procedure —
  the earlier `workersClient.jobs.trigger({ idempotencyKey })` shape did not exist; the
  idempotency key travels in the payload). Draft results carry their lines again
  (`DraftResult.lines` restored, fed from the billing client's typed output).
- `domain/runs.ts` — added `listRuns`, `getRun`, `decideRunItem` (idempotent by
  `decide:{runItemId}:{decision}` key, persisted in `RunDecisionRecord`), `getRunConsole`
  (computed/issued/pending/failed totals + monotonic `version` from `updatedAt`).
- `routers/v1.ts` — the scaffold stub (in-memory seeded records, `RunsListItemV1`) is gone; all
  seven run-console procedures bind to the domain with `serializeRun`/`serializeRunItem` in
  `routers/mappers.ts` (Dates → ISO, Decimals → money strings via the money lib).
- Path-parameter procedures now carry `{ id }` in their input schemas (`decide`, `issue`) —
  oRPC binds `{id}` from the input, and the scaffold-era split caused TS2339s.

### D3 — Web billing data layer (factory → query utils)

`createQueryFactories` only exposes flat contract shapes (its type maps
`ContractProcedureNames` over top-level keys and its runtime builds one action per top-level
key), so the nested billing contract cannot drive it. `apps/ledgerline-web/lib/billing.ts` now
uses the documented `createServiceQueryUtils(billingClient, { path: ['billing'] })`, which
preserves nested inference (`billingQueryUtils.invoices.list.queryOptions({ input })`). The
runs/webhooks libs keep `createQueryFactories` (their contracts are flat) — no mixed shapes
within one data layer.

### Verification

`deno task check` → 0 type errors (was 13 + scaffold drift); `deno task deps:verify` → 550
packages verified (the earlier failure was a stale node_modules materialization mid-task, not a
dependency defect); `deno fmt` applied to touched files; `deno lint` clean on all touched files
(the 77 pre-existing problems are the stock `webhooks.contract.ts` no-slow-types, untouched).
